From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:42:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] docs: expose provider-family enforcement policy
X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: expose and document provider-family execution allowlist
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-provider-policy
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1002-personal-openrouter-eu.patch

Patch intent:
Expose the provider.allowed_providers execution policy in the generated default
configuration and define how it composes with model_picker_providers.

Why it exists:
The typed policy and runtime enforcement foundation is supplied by patch 1002 so
that OpenRouter EU and all shared-slot identities compile as one coherent unit.
This follow-on owns the user-facing policy contract: empty or absent means
unrestricted, a non-empty list fails closed for unknown identities, and picker
filtering may only narrow execution permission. It does not duplicate runtime
identity or enforcement logic.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs documents canonical provider
families, accepted aliases, separate OpenRouter and OpenRouter EU families, and
the relationship between allowed_providers and model_picker_providers. The
parsed setting, catalog projection, switching, dispatch, fallback, remote route,
and persisted-route enforcement points are provided by its required 1002
foundation.

Update guidance:
Keep allowed_providers an execution boundary rather than a presentation-only
filter. Preserve empty-list legacy behavior, fail closed for non-empty invalid
configuration, warn about unknown values, and keep picker policy strictly
narrower. If generated configuration moves, retain this contract next to other
provider policy settings and continue depending on patch 1002 typed identity.

Validation:
./scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-provider-core provider_family_policy_ --lib
./scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base provider_route_ --lib
./scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base model_routes_memo_reprojects_when_provider_allowlist_changes --lib
---
diff --git a/crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs b/crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs
index 5beedb69dc0b733d565b767c8493fc03eafd5f98..a8aa4c1b0b2aa6cbca3cd70e4fa0586e2efb468a 100644
--- a/crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs
+++ b/crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs
@@ -358,6 +358,15 @@ tool_profile = "acp"
 # `claude` and `anthropic-api` are distinct providers with distinct credentials.
 # See docs/AUTH_CREDENTIAL_SOURCES.md for where each credential lives.
 # default_provider = "copilot"
+# Optional execution allowlist for provider families. This policy is enforced
+# for model switching, persisted routes, dispatch, and failover, not just picker
+# visibility. Empty or unset keeps all providers enabled. A non-empty list with
+# only unknown entries fails closed. Unknown entries are warned about and denied.
+# Canonical families: jcode, claude, openai, openrouter, openrouter-eu,
+# grok-build, openai-compatible, copilot, cursor, bedrock, gemini, antigravity.
+# Common aliases such as anthropic, chatgpt, aws-bedrock, and grok are accepted.
+# openrouter and openrouter-eu are intentionally separate families.
+# allowed_providers = ["claude", "openrouter-eu"]
 # OpenAI reasoning effort (none|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh|max)
 openai_reasoning_effort = "low"
 # Anthropic reasoning effort for Claude reasoning models (none|low|medium|high|xhigh|max)
@@ -387,7 +396,9 @@ cross_provider_failover = "countdown"
 # provider labels ("openai", "anthropic", "copilot", "openrouter", ...), route
 # api methods ("claude-oauth", "openai-compatible:myprofile"), or bare
 # openai-compatible profile ids ("myprofile"). The active model's routes always
-# stay visible. Unset or empty = show everything.
+# stay visible. Unset or empty = show everything permitted by allowed_providers.
+# This option can narrow picker visibility, but never grants execution that
+# allowed_providers denies.
 # model_picker_providers = ["myprofile", "openrouter"]
 # Max seconds to wait for streaming data before timing out a request with no
 # data received. Raise this for slow reasoning models (e.g. DeepSeek) that think
